# onnxruntime-node ships an optional CUDA execution provider, and its install
# script tries to download a GPU build before checking whether the machine has
# a GPU. On a plain cloud VM that request 404s and takes the whole `npm ci`
# down with it -- which stops the deploy, not just that one package.
#
# Nothing in this project uses ONNX. It arrives under @iwsdk/reference, the
# editor's code-search tool, which the server never runs. Skipping the CUDA
# download leaves the package installed and working; only the GPU execution
# provider is omitted.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
